**H1: Why Your AI Investment Isn't Showing Up in the Numbers (And How to Fix That)**

---

**H2: You're Using the Wrong Scorecard**

Most organizations measure AI the same way they measured software deployments in the 1990s — cost savings and headcount reduction. That framework was built for a different kind of investment. Applied to AI, it captures only the shallowest layer of value and guarantees disappointment.

Section notes: Open with the CFO scenario. Introduce the three-dimension framework (operational efficiency, strategic differentiation, organizational intelligence). Make the measurement mismatch the diagnosis, not a criticism.

